## Step 5 — Sequencing Checklist

```
1. Pre-work: DB backup, transaction-boundary map, flag sequence-ID race condition (log only, don't fix)
2. Tier 1 (reads): migrate all 7 functions with parallel-run diffing, cut over one at a time, 
   regression test after each cutover
3. Tier 2 (single-table writes): migrate approve_one, reject_one, approve_all with staging 
   before/after diff testing, cut over one at a time, regression test after each
4. Tier 3 (multi-statement transactional writes): migrate mrr_submission_node, evaluate_and_route, 
   auto_verifier_node — one function at a time, staging before/after diff testing INCLUDING 
   deliberate failure-injection testing for rollback correctness, cut over one at a time, 
   full regression test after each
5. Final: run complete MRR regression checklist one more time, confirm no raw SQL remains 
   in nodes.py / approver_react_agent.py / tools.py / creator_agent.py's remnants (already deleted)
```

Do not compress this into "migrate everything then test once." Every cutover gets its own regression pass, same discipline as Phase 1 and the RMS refactor.

