## What to Tell Your AI to Start

> "We're beginning Phase 2, Tier 1 only — the 7 read-only SELECT functions. First, produce a transaction-boundary map for all Tier 2/3 functions so we understand atomicity requirements before we get there, and flag the sequence-ID generation pattern as a known race condition to log as a separate backlog item, not fix now. Then, for each Tier 1 function, implement the DAO method as an exact copy of the existing SQL, and wire dual-execution parallel-run logging so we can verify equivalence before cutting over. Do not touch Tier 2 or Tier 3 yet."

Get Tier 1 fully verified and cut over before even discussing Tier 2. This will feel slow. That's the point — this is the tier of your codebase where "fast and slightly wrong" costs you a corrupted requisition, not a failed test.